{"type":"plan","title":"風鈴の願い","logline":"夏休み、京都のおばあちゃんの家で鳴らなくなった江戸風鈴が、少女の願いと夜風で再び音を取り戻す温かな物語。","shots":[{"index":1,"shotType":"Wide shot","description":"Daytime wide view of the grandmother's porch: yui walks up the stone steps in her blue yukata, grandma stands at the rail smiling, the silent Edo wind chime hangs from the bamboo hook. Light: bright morning sun.","mode":"still","dialogue":"夏休み、ゆいは、京都のおばあちゃんの家に、遊びに来ました。","cites":[]},{"index":2,"shotType":"Medium shot","description":"Medium framing on the porch rail: the Edo wind chime hangs motionless, its glass bulb catching the morning light. Grandma glances toward it, curious. Light: morning sun.","mode":"still","dialogue":"縁側には、古い江戸風鈴が、ひとつ下がっていますが、もう、音が鳴りません。","cites":[]},{"index":3,"shotType":"Close-up","description":"Close‑up on grandma's face as she speaks, yui visible over her shoulder listening. Grandma smiles gently, yui looks left with surprise. Light: morning sun.","mode":"still","dialogue":"「おじいちゃんと買った風鈴なの」と、おばあちゃんは、言いました。","cites":[]},{"index":4,"shotType":"Wide shot","description":"Evening wide shot of the Gion festival street: paper lanterns glow amber, food stalls line the stone lane. Yui and grandma walk side by side in yukata, lantern light painting their faces. Light: golden dusk.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"夕方、二人は、浴衣を着て、祇園祭の宵山へ、出かけました。","cites":[]},{"index":5,"shotType":"Pan","description":"Slow pan across the lantern‑lit street, yui turns her head right, eyes wide with wonder at the glowing chochin. Light: golden dusk.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"提灯の灯る通りには、屋台が、ずらりと並んでいます。","cites":[]},{"index":6,"shotType":"Close-up","description":"Close‑up at a wind‑chime stall: yui's hand holds a blue tanzaku strip, choosing it among colorful chimes. The stall's noren flaps gently. Light: golden dusk.","mode":"still","dialogue":"風鈴の屋台で、ゆいは、青い短冊を、一枚選びました。","cites":[]},{"index":7,"shotType":"Medium shot","description":"Night interior of grandmother's house: yui sits at a low table, writing a wish on the blue tanzaku by lamp light. The room is quiet, tatami visible. Light: night, lamp glow.","mode":"still","dialogue":"夜、家に帰ると、ゆいは、短冊に、願いごとを書きました。","cites":[]},{"index":8,"shotType":"Close-up","description":"Insert detail of the blue tanzaku: the handwritten wish reads “おばあちゃんの風鈴が、また、鳴りますように”. Yui's fingers rest on the paper. Light: night, lamp glow.","mode":"still","dialogue":"「おばあちゃんの風鈴が、また、鳴りますように」。","cites":[]},{"index":9,"shotType":"Medium shot","description":"Night on the porch: yui kneels to tie the tanzaku to the silent wind chime, a gentle night breeze stirs the bamboo leaves. Grandma watches from the side. Light: night, lantern glow.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"ゆいが、短冊を風鈴に結ぶと、夜風が、そっと吹きました。","cites":[]},{"index":10,"shotType":"Close-up","description":"Close‑up on the wind chime as the night wind passes: the glass bulb trembles and a clear “ちりん” rings out. Yui looks right, eyes bright with surprise. Light: night, lantern glow.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"ちりん。風鈴が、ひさしぶりに、鳴りました。","cites":[]},{"index":11,"shotType":"Wide shot","description":"Final wide shot of the porch at night: grandma gently wipes a tear, then pats yui's head. The wind chime sways softly, its sound lingering. Light: night, lantern glow.","mode":"still","dialogue":"おばあちゃんは、そっと涙をふいて、ゆいの頭を、なでました。","cites":[]}]}
